WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.491 --> 00:00:02.860
(gunshots echoing)

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.140
- [Yaroslav] There was occasional
firing at the perimeter

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.148
because crowds tried
to breach the airport.

00:00:08.148 --> 00:00:11.573
(distant chatter)

00:00:11.573 --> 00:00:13.047
A couple of times, there
were warnings of attack

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:16.623
so we put on the body armor
and helmets and take cover.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.555
I spent almost five years as
our Bureau Chief in Kabul.

00:00:21.555 --> 00:00:24.222
(pensive music)

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.960
The Italian embassy had arranged

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.990
a repatriation flight and the initial idea

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.450
was that there would be a meeting

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.030
at the airport gate, where
they would direct you in

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.290
and then you go there.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.520
But the airport was already surrounded

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.000
by thousands and thousands of people

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.800
and the road to the
airport was non-passable,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.090
so they had to fly everyone they could

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.178
by helicopter from the
American Embassy compound.

00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:04.355
It's just next door to the Italian one.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.022
(pensive music)

00:01:09.036 --> 00:01:09.983
There was no food.

00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:12.080
I was just on my phone writing.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.680
I'm lucky that I managed to find

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.277
an outlet for power to charge up my phone.

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.480
(yelling)

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.690
Later in the day,

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.378
when crowds got even bigger and rowdier,

00:01:24.378 --> 00:01:27.498
the US Marines started
to shoot in the air.

00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:29.354
(gunshots echoing)

00:01:29.354 --> 00:01:31.937
(wind blowing)

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.130
(chatter)

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.180
US Marine or quick reaction force

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.200
was called in to deal
with the situation of

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.843
hundreds of Afghan civilians

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.570
trying to board and
idling (indistinguishable)

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.250
plane that was on the tarmac.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.020
It eventually took off
with about 600 people

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.220
in there packed like sardines.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.910
The military airport doesn't
have any normal facilities.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.640
You don't have these boarding
vehicles or the racks

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.890
so there was this emergency ladder

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.300
that comes with the aircraft itself

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.530
and you have to climb up,

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:13.620
which is...

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.230
for people that have strollers

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.228
for babies was quite difficult.

00:02:18.228 --> 00:02:20.895
(pensive music)

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.433
We were waiting

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.100
because a lot of the Afghan staff,

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.520
a lot of the Italians were not able

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.353
to make it to the airport.

00:02:31.353 --> 00:02:32.310
They were stranded outside.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.180
They were stranded in the city.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.160
The checkpoints were closed.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.910
And a lot of people didn't make it.

